   "source": [
    "# Cell2location — Deconvolución espacial HGSOC (ATLAS_MSK)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Muestras:** GIN63, GIN65, GIN67, GIN71 (Visium, HGSOC)  \n",
    "**Atlas de referencia:** `ATLAS_MSK.h5ad` (scRNA-seq, MSK SPECTRUM, 37 subtipos finos vía `cluster_label`)\n",
    "\n",
    "Este notebook procesa las 4 muestras juntas (necesario para entrenar una única\n",
    "firma de referencia y un único modelo de mapeo espacial), a diferencia de los\n",
    "scripts anteriores del pipeline, que son uno por paciente. Al final, los\n",
    "resultados se reparten de vuelta a cada muestra y se guardan como\n",
    "`h5ad_outputs/{SAMPLE}_cell2location.h5ad`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Input:** `h5ad_outputs/{SAMPLE}_infercnv.h5ad` (las 4 muestras)  \n",
    "**Output:** `h5ad_outputs/{SAMPLE}_cell2location.h5ad` (una por muestra)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Se puede volver a ejecutar sin re-entrenar nada.** Al principio se comprueba\n",
    "si ya existen los resultados guardados en disco (firma de referencia y mapeo\n",
    "espacial). Si existen, se cargan directamente y el notebook salta las celdas\n",
    "de entrenamiento (que son las que tardan horas / necesitan GPU). Para forzar\n",
    "un reentrenamiento, cambiar `FORCE_RETRAIN_REFERENCE` o `FORCE_RETRAIN_C2L` a\n",
    "`True` en la sección de parámetros.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5f771726",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0. Librerías y configuración de entorno"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "77d9e746",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import scanpy as sc\n",
    "import anndata as ad\n",
    "import matplotlib as mpl\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from matplotlib.patches import Wedge\n",
    "from matplotlib.lines import Line2D\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from scipy.stats import zscore, entropy\n",
    "from collections import defaultdict\n",
    "\n",
    "import cell2location\n",
    "from cell2location.models import RegressionModel, Cell2location\n",
    "from cell2location.utils.filtering import filter_genes\n",
    "from cell2location import run_colocation\n",
    "\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "# Fix conocido de compatibilidad scvi-tools/rich: view_anndata_setup() llama a\n",
    "# rich.pretty.pprint(), que no siempre se carga solo con \"import rich\".\n",
    "import rich.pretty\n",
    "\n",
    "torch.set_float32_matmul_precision('high')\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "sc.settings.verbosity = 1\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "\n",
    "USE_GPU = torch.cuda.is_available()\n",
    "print(f\"GPU disponible: {USE_GPU}\")\n",
    "if USE_GPU:\n",
    "    print(torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n",
    "ACCELERATOR = \"gpu\" if USE_GPU else \"cpu\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "08f02b21",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Parámetros, rutas y modos de ejecución\n",
    "\n",
    "`FORCE_RETRAIN_REFERENCE` y `FORCE_RETRAIN_C2L` controlan si se reentrena desde cero\n",
    "o si se reutilizan los resultados ya guardados en `SIGNATURE_DIR` / `DECONV_DIR`.\n",
    "Por defecto están en `False`: si los ficheros ya existen, el notebook los carga y\n",
    "salta directamente a la parte de análisis y visualización.\n",
    "\n",
    "Si se reentrena la firma de referencia, se fuerza también el reentrenamiento del\n",
    "mapeo espacial (`c2l_needed`), porque un cambio en la firma invalida el mapeo\n",
    "anterior (estaría comparando spots con una firma de referencia distinta).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# Parámetros del notebook\n",
    "# --------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "# Atlas de referencia (scRNA-seq, MSK SPECTRUM) -- version con cluster_label (subtipos finos)\n",
    "ATLAS_PATH = \"/home/imartinezle/Spatial_transcriptomics/ATLAS_MSK.h5ad\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Muestras Visium: se lee la salida del script 04 (InferCNV), que ya trae\n",
    "# acumuladas las columnas de los scripts anteriores (Layer_patologo, clustering,\n",
    "# ESTIMATE, InferCNV)\n",
    "SAMPLES = [\"GIN63\", \"GIN65\", \"GIN67\", \"GIN71\"]\n",
    "H5AD_DIR = \"/home/imartinezle/h5ad_outputs/\"\n",
    "VIS_PATHS = {s: f\"{H5AD_DIR}{s}_infercnv.h5ad\" for s in SAMPLES}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Rutas de salida. El modelo entrenado (firma + mapeo) no es una figura ni un\n",
    "# h5ad del pipeline, es un artefacto intermedio de cell2location -- se queda\n",
    "# en su propia carpeta de trabajo.\n",
    "WORK_DIR = \"/home/imartinezle/Resultados_R/cell2location_ATLAS_MSK/\"\n",
    "SIGNATURE_DIR = os.path.join(WORK_DIR, \"signature\")\n",
    "DECONV_DIR = os.path.join(WORK_DIR, \"deconvolution\")\n",
    "FIG_DIR_COMPARATIVA = \"/home/imartinezle/Figuras/cell2location_comparativa/\"\n",
    "for d in (SIGNATURE_DIR, DECONV_DIR, FIG_DIR_COMPARATIVA, H5AD_DIR):\n",
    "    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "INFER_AVER_PATH = os.path.join(SIGNATURE_DIR, \"infer_aver.csv\")\n",
    "C2L_H5AD_PATH = os.path.join(DECONV_DIR, \"cell2location_all_samples.h5ad\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Columnas del atlas de referencia\n",
    "REF_CELL_TYPE_KEY = \"cluster_label\"     # 37 subtipos finos (Cancer.cell.1, CD8.T.cytotoxic, etc.)\n",
    "REF_BATCH_KEY = \"donor_id\"              # 10X reaction / paciente\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filtro de sitio anatómico del atlas\n",
    "TUMOR_SUPERSITES = [\"Adnexa\", \"Omentum\"]\n",
    "MIN_CELLS_PER_TYPE = 50\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filtrado de genes para la firma de referencia\n",
    "CELL_COUNT_CUTOFF = 3\n",
    "CELL_PERCENTAGE_CUTOFF2 = 0.03\n",
    "NONZ_MEAN_CUTOFF = 1.12\n",
    "\n",
    "# Entrenamiento del modelo de regresión (firmas)\n",
    "REF_N_EPOCHS = 100 # Ajustado para evitar overfitting\n",
    "\n",
    "# Entrenamiento de Cell2location (mapeo espacial)\n",
    "C2L_N_EPOCHS = 5000\n",
    "C2L_BATCH_SIZE = 2500          # batch_size finito -- evita el OOM de GPU (None carga todo de golpe)\n",
    "C2L_EARLY_STOPPING_PATIENCE = 500\n",
    "\n",
    "# Nº de tipos celulares principales a mostrar en el \"quesito\" espacial por spot\n",
    "TOP_N_CELLTYPES_PIE = 4\n",
    "\n",
    "# --------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# Modos de ejecucion: reentrenar o cargar de disco\n",
    "# --------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "FORCE_RETRAIN_REFERENCE = False   # True -> reentrena la firma de referencia desde cero\n",
    "FORCE_RETRAIN_C2L = False         # True -> reentrena el mapeo espacial desde cero\n",
    "\n",
    "signature_needed = FORCE_RETRAIN_REFERENCE or not os.path.exists(INFER_AVER_PATH)\n",
    "c2l_needed = FORCE_RETRAIN_C2L or not os.path.exists(C2L_H5AD_PATH) or signature_needed\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Muestras configuradas:\", SAMPLES)\n",
    "print(f\"¿Reentrenar firma de referencia? -> {signature_needed}\")\n",
    "print(f\"¿Reentrenar mapeo espacial (cell2location)? -> {c2l_needed}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "32c66bc0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Firma de referencia (modelo de regresión sobre el atlas scRNA-seq)\n",
    "\n",
    "Esta sección solo se ejecuta si `signature_needed` es `True` (no existe todavía\n",
    "`infer_aver.csv`, o se ha forzado el reentrenamiento). Si ya existe, se salta\n",
    "directamente a la celda de carga del CSV, unas celdas más abajo.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1522f3a5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if signature_needed:\n",
    "    print(\"No se encontró una firma de referencia guardada (o se forzó el reentrenamiento). Entrenando...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # --- 2.1 Carga del atlas y counts crudos -----------------------------\n",
    "    adata_ref = sc.read_h5ad(ATLAS_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Los counts crudos están en .raw (adata_ref.X del atlas de CxG viene normalizado)\n",
    "    raw_adata = adata_ref.raw.to_adata()\n",
    "    raw_adata.var_names = raw_adata.var['feature_name'].astype(str).values\n",
    "    raw_adata.var_names_make_unique()\n",
    "    adata_ref.X = raw_adata[:, adata_ref.var_names].X.copy()\n",
    "    print(f\"Shape del atlas: {adata_ref.shape}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # --- 2.2 Filtrado por sitio anatómico tumoral ------------------------\n",
    "    # Nos quedamos con las localizaciones más representativas del tumor\n",
    "    # primario / metástasis peritoneal.\n",
    "    mask = adata_ref.obs['author_tumor_supersite'].isin(TUMOR_SUPERSITES)\n",
    "    adata_ref = adata_ref[mask].copy()\n",
    "    print(f\"Células tras filtrar por author_tumor_supersite {TUMOR_SUPERSITES}: {adata_ref.n_obs}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # --- 2.3 Descartar tipos celulares con muy pocas células (p.ej. \"Other\") ---\n",
    "    counts_before = adata_ref.obs[REF_CELL_TYPE_KEY].value_counts()\n",
    "    valid_types = counts_before[counts_before >= MIN_CELLS_PER_TYPE].index.tolist()\n",
    "    adata_ref = adata_ref[adata_ref.obs[REF_CELL_TYPE_KEY].isin(valid_types)].copy()\n",
    "    adata_ref.obs[REF_CELL_TYPE_KEY] = adata_ref.obs[REF_CELL_TYPE_KEY].cat.remove_unused_categories()\n",
    "    print(f\"Tipos celulares retenidos: {list(adata_ref.obs[REF_CELL_TYPE_KEY].cat.categories)}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Firma de referencia ya calculada -> se reutiliza (no se toca el atlas).\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e4ed88ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.1 Filtrado de genes informativos y entrenamiento del modelo de regresión"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "dc94ebec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if signature_needed:\n",
    "    selected = filter_genes(\n",
    "        adata_ref,\n",
    "        cell_count_cutoff=CELL_COUNT_CUTOFF,\n",
    "        cell_percentage_cutoff2=CELL_PERCENTAGE_CUTOFF2,\n",
    "        nonz_mean_cutoff=NONZ_MEAN_CUTOFF,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    adata_ref_filt = adata_ref[:, selected].copy()\n",
    "    print(f\"Genes tras filter_genes: {adata_ref_filt.n_vars:,}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    RegressionModel.setup_anndata(\n",
    "        adata=adata_ref_filt,\n",
    "        batch_key=REF_BATCH_KEY,       # 10X reaction / paciente\n",
    "        labels_key=REF_CELL_TYPE_KEY,  # tipo celular\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    mod_ref = RegressionModel(adata_ref_filt)\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        mod_ref.view_anndata_setup()\n",
    "    except AttributeError as e:\n",
    "        print(f\"(Aviso: no se pudo mostrar el resumen de configuración — {e}. No afecta al entrenamiento.)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # precision=32 evita el ValueError de GammaPoisson (rate negativo) por overflow en fp16\n",
    "    mod_ref.train(max_epochs=REF_N_EPOCHS, accelerator=ACCELERATOR, precision=32)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "017ffad9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.2 Diagnóstico del entrenamiento (curva ELBO y control de calidad)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
